-- 0051_tosh_full_report_detail.sql
-- Replace the TOSH summary rows with the measured points, and correct the
-- finding that was raised from the summary alone.
--
-- 0050 had only page 1 of 14: "แสงสว่างแบบใช้สายตามองเฉพาะจุด — ไม่ผ่าน 12 จาก
-- 13 จุด". From that, NCR-256908-002 was graded Major partly on the reasoning
-- that task-specific measurement points are where foreign matter is inspected,
-- which would make it a GHP issue and not only an occupational one.
--
-- The full report shows that reasoning was wrong. All thirteen spot points are
-- งานบันทึกเอกสาร — desk work — in สำนักงานผลิต, บัญชี/การเงิน, บุคคล,
-- ขาย/การตลาด and outside the managing director's office. Not one is a
-- production inspection station. The standard applied to them is 400–500 lux,
-- which is an office desk criterion, and the twelve failures run 105–340 lux.
-- Real, legal, and remediable, but not food safety.
--
-- What IS food-safety relevant is the single AREA failure the summary buried:
-- จุดแพ็ค 2 measured 268 lux average against a 300 lux standard, with the cause
-- recorded on the spot as พบหลอดไฟชำรุด. That is a packing station, and the fix
-- is a lamp. The production room itself passed at 325/166.
--
-- So the grading moves to Minor and the description says what was actually
-- measured. Inferring the character of thirteen measurements from a summary
-- count was the mistake; the detail pages were available for the asking.
--
-- Noise and heat both passed and are recorded for completeness — including that
-- the heat reading was taken while it was raining, which an auditor comparing it
-- against a hot-season complaint would want to know.

